outputs.L1:
A method for fabricating a three-dimensional object, the method comprising:

a) positioning a layer of particles over a build plate;

b) exposing the layer of particles to a first laser beam having a first set of beam characteristics, thereby heating the layer sufficiently to fuse at least a portion of the particles together to form a build layer;

c) exposing a first region of either i) the layer of particles or ii) the build layer to a second laser beam having a second set of beam characteristics to provide a first temperature profile for the first region; and

d) exposing a second region of either i) the layer of particles or ii) the build layer to a third laser beam having a third set of beam characteristics to provide a second temperature profile for the second region, the second temperature profile being different from the first temperature profile,

wherein both the first region and the second region are in the layer of particles, or both the first region and the second region are in the build layer.

counterfactuals.output:
1. A method of additive manufacturing, comprising:

depositing a layer of powder material on a build surface to form a powder bed;

directing a first laser beam onto the layer of powder material along a build path to selectively fuse particles of the powder material and form at least a portion of a build layer of a three-dimensional article;

directing a second laser beam onto a first region of the powder bed associated with the build layer to generate a first temperature profile in the first region; and

directing a third laser beam onto a second region of the powder bed associated with the build layer, the second region being different from the first region, to generate a second temperature profile in the second region,

wherein the first temperature profile is different from the second temperature profile.

1. A method of forming a three-dimensional object, the method comprising:

depositing a layer of particulate build material on a build plate;

selectively heating, in accordance with object data, a portion of the layer of particulate build material to form a fused region corresponding to a cross-section of the three-dimensional object;

performing a first additional laser exposure on a first region of the layer, the first additional laser exposure being controlled to apply a first temperature profile to the first region; and

performing a second additional laser exposure on a second region of the layer, different from the first region, the second additional laser exposure being controlled to apply a second temperature profile to the second region;

wherein the first temperature profile is different from the second temperature profile.

1. A powder-bed additive manufacturing method, comprising:

   depositing a layer of particulate build material over a build area;

   selectively irradiating, with a first laser beam, a first region of the layer in accordance with build data corresponding to a cross-section of a three-dimensional article, thereby at least partially consolidating the particulate build material in the first region;

   irradiating, with a second laser beam, a second region of the layer, the second laser beam having a first set of beam characteristics including at least one of a first wavelength, a first power, a first spot size, a first beam shape, a first scanning speed, a first energy density, or a first temporal modulation profile;

   irradiating, with a third laser beam, a third region of the layer, the third laser beam having a second set of beam characteristics different from the first set of beam characteristics, the second set of beam characteristics including at least one of a second wavelength, a second power, a second spot size, a second beam shape, a second scanning speed, a second energy density, or a second temporal modulation profile;

   wherein the second region and the third region are different regions of the same deposited layer or build layer; and

   repeating the depositing and irradiating steps for a plurality of layers to form the three-dimensional article.
